diff --git a/docs/business-rules.md b/docs/business-rules.md
index 7a3126a..9e88a80 100644
--- a/docs/business-rules.md
+++ b/docs/business-rules.md
@@ -64,6 +64,17 @@ ## User Administration
 | Remove account | Admin, owner | Not applicable to owner while being owner. |
 | Remove user | Admin, owner | Cannot remove the owner; employees lose immediate access to the entity. |
 | Assign role | Admin, owner | Users are **separated by role**; employees receive granular permissions, not admin/owner role. |
+| Invite user | Admin, owner | Invites an e-mail with role `admin` or `employee` (never `owner`). Membership exists only after the invitee accepts. |
+
+### Invitations
+
+- The members page is manager-only (owner and admin). Employees get 403.
+- An invite expires **7 days** after it is sent. A **pending** invite is one that is neither accepted nor expired.
+- An e-mail may have only one pending invite per entity. An expired or already accepted invite may be replaced by a new one.
+- Only the invitee (e-mail match, case-insensitive) can accept or decline. Accepting creates the membership with the invited role, and an accepted invite is idempotent. Declining deletes the invite.
+- Managers can cancel pending invites. Each manager may send at most **10 successful invites per hour** per entity; invalid input does not count.
+- An e-mail that already belongs to a member cannot be invited.
+- Existing members' roles are changed from the member details modal (explicit "save role"). Removal requires a confirmation and keeps the owner and the last manager protected.
 
 ## Queue and Tickets
 
